      "description": "[This course is offered via asynchronous online mode. Students should register the course via KEEP, a CUHK eLearning platform where the course materials are uploaded.]\n\nThis online self-learning course invites students without prior knowledge of German to explore some basic features of the German language and culture through a virtual journey. Based on texts, audio and video input, and interactive tasks, students will be able to practice both spoken and written German. This course serves as a taster course for students who may consider taking German courses at CUHK in the future.",
      "enrollment_requirement": "Not for students who have taken GERM1000,2000,2001,2050,3000,3001,3002,3050,3051or4001\nFrom 2023-24, students can only earn up to 2 units of these courses: CLCP1001,CLCP1101,CLCC1001,CLCC1101,JASP1350,HKSL1001,SPAN1001,GERM1001,KORE1001,FREN1001",
      "course_attributes": "Virtual Teaching & Learning Course",
      "academic_career": "Undergraduate",
      "grading_basis": "Pass (P)/Fail (U)",
      "component": "Lecture",
      "campus": "Main Campus",
      "academic_group": "Dept of Linguistics & Mod Lang",
      "academic_org": "Dept of Linguistics & Mod Lang",
      "learning_outcomes": "Upon completion of the course, students are expected to be able to\n• understand basic features of the German language;\n• understand selected information related to German culture;\n• identify “international” loanwords (e.g. “kindergarten”) as a helpful means to understand vocabulary;\n• recognise the relationship between English and German in terms of vocabulary;\n• apply basic structures to simple everyday situations, e.g. greetings, introducing oneself and others, expressing food preferences and dislikes, and talking about hobbies;\n• implement independent learning as part of their learning experience.",
      "assessment_types": {}
    },
