      "description": "This course aims to further enhance students’ communication skills in the four language domains listening, speaking, reading and writing. Students are expected to communicate confidently in a wider range of social interactions including more formal situations and simple professional contexts as well as reporting past events and sharing experience. At the end of this course, students will have completed a proficiency level comparable to level A1 of the Common European Framework of Reference for Languages (CEFR).",
      "enrollment_requirement": "1. Not for students who have taken GERM3000,3001,3002,3050, 3051 or 4001\n2. Prerequisite: GERM2000 or 2050",
      "course_attributes": "",
      "academic_career": "Undergraduate",
      "grading_basis": "Graded",
      "component": "Classwork",
      "campus": "Main Campus",
      "academic_group": "Dept of Linguistics & Mod Lang",
      "academic_org": "Dept of Linguistics & Mod Lang",
      "learning_outcomes": "Upon completion of the course, the student should be able to deal with a range of situations in German such as\n• discussing one’s living situation;\n• discussing holiday and vacation;\n• reporting about Germany and one’s own country;\n• talking about health and nutrition;\n• talking about events of the past.",
      "assessment_types": {
        "Essay test or exam": "55",
        "Others": "25",
        "Presentation": "20"
      }
